  <!-- §01 — Overview -->
  <section class="section" id="overview" aria-labelledby="overview-label">
    <p class="section-label" id="overview-label">§01 · Overview</p>
    <div class="overview-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <p><b>OpenAgentSafety</b> evaluates whether frontier AI agents behave safely when given access to real tools in realistic workplace scenarios. Each task places an agent in a high-risk situation — with access to file systems, terminals, web browsers, and messaging platforms — where it faces pressure to perform unsafe actions through direct instructions or adversarial NPC interactions.</p>
        <p>A multi-layer evaluation pipeline combines deterministic rule-based checks with LLM-as-judge assessments to detect unsafe behaviors ranging from credential leaks to financial data manipulation.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="glance" aria-label="At a glance">
        <p class="glance-label mono">At a glance</p>
        <dl class="glance-list">
          <div class="glance-row"><dt>Scenarios</dt><dd><b>361</b></dd></div>
          <div class="glance-row"><dt>Models</dt><dd><b>5</b> frontier</dd></div>
          <div class="glance-row"><dt>Attack Vectors</dt><dd><b>5</b></dd></div>
          <div class="glance-row"><dt>Task Structures</dt><dd><b>3</b></dd></div>
          <div class="glance-row"><dt>Infrastructure</dt><dd><b>4</b> services</dd></div>
          <div class="glance-row"><dt>Eval Layers</dt><dd><b>2</b> active</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

