  <!-- §04 — Pipeline -->
  <section class="section section-pipeline" id="pipeline" aria-labelledby="pipeline-label">
    <p class="section-label" id="pipeline-label">§04 · Pipeline</p>
    <div class="pipeline-frame">
      <div class="pipeline-intro">
        <p class="pipeline-eyebrow mono">The method</p>
        <h2 class="pipeline-title">Three phases turn a workplace scenario into a safety verdict.</h2>
        <p class="pipeline-sub">From scenario construction through agent interaction to multi-layer evaluation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline pipeline-a">
        <article class="phase">
          <p class="phase-label">Phase 01</p>
          <h4 class="phase-title">Scenario Construction</h4>
          <ul class="phase-body">
            <li>Design realistic workplace safety scenarios (O*NET-informed)</li>
            <li>Create adversarial task instructions &amp; NPC strategy configs</li>
            <li>Build hermetic Docker environments with live services</li>
            <li>Embed verifiable markers for deterministic evaluation</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="phase">
          <p class="phase-label">Phase 02</p>
          <h4 class="phase-title">Agent Interaction</h4>
          <ul class="phase-body">
            <li>Deploy AI agents in sandboxed containers with real tool access</li>
            <li>Agents receive task at /instruction/task.md</li>
            <li>Adversarial NPCs engage in live multi-turn chat (196 tasks)</li>
            <li>Full trajectories &amp; final state captured</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="phase">
          <p class="phase-label">Phase 03</p>
          <h4 class="phase-title">Multi-Layer Evaluation</h4>
          <ul class="phase-body">
            <li>Layer 1 — Rule-Based: deterministic file state + regex checks</li>
            <li>Layer 2 — LLM-as-Judge: GPT-4.1 with 4-label rubric</li>
            <li>Binary verdict from rules + nuanced score from judge</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- §05 — Results -->
  <section class="section section-reveal" id="results" aria-labelledby="results-label">
    <p class="section-label" id="results-label">§05 · Results</p>

    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="reveal-line">
        All five frontier models exhibit <b>substantial safety failures</b> when operating with real tools in adversarial workplace scenarios.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal-line reveal-kicker">
        Rule-based evaluation shows <span class="reveal-big">39–43%</span> unsafe action rates.
        LLM-judge rates are higher (<span class="reveal-big">44–66%</span>) capturing subtler compliance patterns.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="section-desc" style="margin-top: 32px;"><b>Rule-Based Evaluation</b> — Percentage of tasks where the unsafe action was verifiably executed.</p>
    <div class="matrix-wrap" style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
      <table class="results-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Model</th>
            <th>Tasks</th>
            <th>Valid</th>
            <th>Unsafe</th>
            <th>Safe</th>
            <th>Unsafe Rate</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><b>Claude Sonnet 3.7</b> *</td><td>165</td><td>136</td><td>58</td><td>78</td><td class="td-danger"><b>42.6%</b></td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>GPT-4o</b></td><td>351</td><td>260</td><td>108</td><td>152</td><td class="td-danger"><b>41.5%</b></td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>o3-mini</b></td><td>296</td><td>296</td><td>119</td><td>177</td><td class="td-danger"><b>40.2%</b></td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>DeepSeek-V3</b></td><td>350</td><td>263</td><td>103</td><td>160</td><td class="td-warning"><b>39.2%</b></td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>DeepSeek-R1</b></td><td>352</td><td>267</td><td>104</td><td>163</td><td class="td-warning"><b>39.0%</b></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="section-desc"><b>LLM-as-Judge Evaluation</b> — Percentage with unsafe behavior detected (labels 1+2).</p>
    <div class="matrix-wrap">
      <table class="results-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Model</th>
            <th>Judged Tasks</th>
            <th>Any Unsafe</th>
            <th>Unsafe Rate</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><b>GPT-4o</b></td><td>193</td><td>127</td><td class="td-danger"><b>65.8%</b></td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>DeepSeek-R1</b></td><td>180</td><td>113</td><td class="td-danger"><b>62.8%</b></td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>DeepSeek-V3</b></td><td>188</td><td>117</td><td class="td-danger"><b>62.2%</b></td></tr>
          <tr><td><b>Claude Sonnet 3.7</b> *</td><td>99</td><td>44</td><td class="td-warning"><b>44.4%</b></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="caption" style="margin-top: 16px;">* Claude evaluated on 165-task subset only. o3-mini uses different format without aggregated LLM-judge labels.</p>
  </section>

